    <dashboard name='Story 1' type='storyboard'>
      <layout-options>
        <title>
          <formatted-text>
            <run bold='true' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>Analyzing NASA’s Near-Earth Objects (1910–2024)</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </title>
      </layout-options>
      <style>
        <style-rule element='story-point-caption'>
          <format attr='width' value='246' />
        </style-rule>
      </style>
      <size maxheight='768' maxwidth='1366' minheight='768' minwidth='1366' preset-index='0' sizing-mode='fixed' />
      <zones>
        <zone h='100000' id='2' type-v2='layout-basic' w='100000' x='0' y='0'>
          <zone h='97916' id='18' param='vert' removable='false' type-v2='layout-flow' w='98828' x='586' y='1042'>
            <zone h='5730' id='19' type-v2='title' w='98828' x='586' y='1042'>
              <zone-style>
                <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
                <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
                <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
                <format attr='margin' value='4' />
              </zone-style>
            </zone>
            <zone h='92186' id='16' param='vert' removable='false' type-v2='layout-flow' w='98828' x='586' y='6772'>
              <zone h='92186' id='1' param='vert' removable='false' type-v2='layout-flow' w='98828' x='586' y='6772'>
                <zone fixed-size='96' h='12500' id='4' is-fixed='true' paired-zone-id='5' removable='false' type-v2='flipboard-nav' w='98828' x='586' y='6772' />
                <zone h='79686' id='5' paired-zone-id='4' removable='false' type-v2='flipboard' w='98828' x='586' y='19272'>
                  <flipboard active-id='5' nav-type='caption' show-nav-arrows='true'>
                    <story-points>
                      <story-point caption='Overview of NASA NEO Dataset' captured-sheet='Dashboard 2' id='5' />
                      <story-point caption='Top 10 Closest Encounters with Earth' captured-sheet='Top 10 closest' id='8' />
                      <story-point caption='Hazardous Objects Over Time' captured-sheet='Haz per yr and dist' id='9' />
                      <story-point caption='Yearly Velocity Trends by Hazard Status' captured-sheet='Yrly vel trends' id='10' />
                      <story-point caption='Cumulative Hazardous Objects' captured-sheet='Dashboard 3' id='11' />
                    </story-points>
                  </flipboard>
                </zone>
              </zone>
            </zone>
          </zone>
          <zone-style>
            <format attr='border-color' value='#000000' />
            <format attr='border-style' value='none' />
            <format attr='border-width' value='0' />
            <format attr='margin' value='8' />
          </zone-style>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' forceUpdate='true' h='25000' id='11' story-point-id='5' type-v2='text' w='50625' x='25563' y='39222'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontname='Tableau Regular'>Analysis of more than 330,000 asteroids recorded by NASA.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
            <run fontname='Tableau Regular'>Focus: distance from Earth, relative velocity, and hazardous classification.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;&#10;</run>
            <run fontname='Tableau Regular'>The goal is to identify patterns in proximity, speed, and risk potential of Near-Earth Objects.</run>
            <run>Æ&#10;</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' forceUpdate='true' h='3556' id='14' story-point-id='5' type-v2='text' w='41938' x='28875' y='30667'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontname='Tableau Regular' fontsize='16'>NASA Near-Earth Objects Dataset (1910–2024)</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' h='3778' hidden='true' id='20' story-point-id='8' type-v2='text' w='31250' x='24563' y='21333'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#252525' fontname='Roboto' fontsize='18' lmargin='555' rmargin='555'>Top 10 closest encounters with Earth</run>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='18' lmargin='555' rmargin='555'>Æ&#10;</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' h='26000' hidden='true' id='21' story-point-id='8' type-v2='text' w='16000' x='45938' y='27111'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book'>These are the most critical passes — all of these objects passed at a distance of less than 15,000 km from Earth. Nearest: 2020 VT4 (6,746 km)</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' forceUpdate='true' h='12333' hidden='true' id='22' story-point-id='9' type-v2='text' w='40313' x='43875' y='25222'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>The increase in the number of detected hazardous objects does not mean that there are more of them — it just means that we are seeing them better. However, the number of ‘Close’ and ‘Very Close’ encounters is constantly increasing.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' forceUpdate='true' h='20222' hidden='true' id='23' story-point-id='10' type-v2='text' w='35063' x='62250' y='68111'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#252525' fontname='Tableau Regular'>Objects classified as &apos;hazardous&apos; are not necessarily the fastest every year, but they have consistently high speeds. The trend shows a slight decrease in non-hazardous objects, but not in dangerous objects.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' h='38556' hidden='true' id='24' story-point-id='11' type-v2='text' w='13375' x='563' y='24556'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>The largest detected Near-Earth Objects vary significantly by year, with diameters ranging from 1 km to over 13 km. The cumulative trend shows a sharp increase after 2000, driven by advances in telescope technology and expanded survey coverage.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
        <zone flipboard-zone-id='5' h='19667' hidden='true' id='25' story-point-id='11' type-v2='text' w='14500' x='62125' y='30667'>
          <formatted-text>
            <run fontalignment='0' fontcolor='#000000' fontname='Benton Sans Book' fontsize='12'>The continuous growth in detected NEOs highlights the importance of planetary defense and sustained monitoring efforts.</run>
          </formatted-text>
        </zone>
      </zones>
      <simple-id uuid='{B4832731-912F-4D01-A8B8-00F757F1A6BB}' />
    </dashboard>
  </dashboards>
